WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.750
Hang a loose wire between
the poles of a strong magnet.

2
00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:05.070
Nothing happens.

3
00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:06.970
Now switch on a current.

4
00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:11.330
The wire leaps sideways, as if an
invisible hand had flicked it.

5
00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:12.750
Nothing touched it.

6
00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:15.630
Reverse the current, and
it leaps the other way.

7
00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:17.550
So what is pushing the wire,

8
00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:20.370
and how can you tell
which way it will jump?

9
00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:23.270
In this mission, you'll
meet the motor effect:

10
00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:26.730
the force on a wire carrying
a current in a magnetic field.

11
00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:30.510
You'll use Fleming's left-hand
rule to predict the direction of

12
00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:31.750
that force.

13
00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:35.300
Your mission: predict which
way the wire will jump.
